WEBVTT

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.320
Strike out!

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.650
He's finally got his game on!

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.160
Strike out!

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.120
Strike out!

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.790
The game between the Hornets and the Coyotes is tied after nine innings,

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.460
and they're heading into extra innings now.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.600
Can you play, Shigeno?

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.560
Yeah, of course.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.990
In fact, I'm finally feeling warmed up after pitching for two innings.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.870
You might end up pitching for a while.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:53.150
Are you going to stay quiet about your condition until you give up a hit or your arm starts hurting?

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.900
Enough with that talk, Keene.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.380
I'm going to do my job without complaint so long as I'm here.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.920
Play!

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.750
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.750
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:19.050
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:19.050
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:24.430
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:24.430
the only thing I truly have

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:29.720
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:29.720
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:35.060
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:35.060
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:40.320
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:40.320
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.700
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.700
I had begun to understand many things

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:51.790
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:51.790
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:57.340
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:57.340
In the junk I've piled up,

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.420
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.420
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:06.720
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:06.720
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:13.020
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:13.020
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:18.650
namida kareru made

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:18.650
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:23.700
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:23.700
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:29.030
namida hareru made

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:29.030
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:34.040
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:34.040
though I may lose my way,

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.880
egakikake no ima

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.880
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.380
kizamu

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:45.130
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.670
akashi

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:45.130
kono te de

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.280
Strike out!

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.420
Strike out!

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.710
Strike out!

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.090
There's his 100 mph!

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.840
Shigeno's struck out all three batters in the tenth inning!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.670
All right!

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.930
That was his sixth consecutive strike out!

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:30.640
Break the Limit

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:30.640
Break the Limit

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.270
Out!

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:41.570
The Hornets' batters went three up, three down in the bottom of the tenth.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:42.830
Oh, man.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:45.010
Three rung up?

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.350
The eleventh inning?!

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.420
Man, Shigeno's amazing.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:57.500
A rookie's made six consecutive strike outs.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.380
Six?!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.570
Hey, which inning did he start in?

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:04.300
Huh?

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.640
Strike out!

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.890
Strike out!

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.190
Strike out!

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.130
That was amazing!

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.880
He's struck out all of the past nine batters!

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.710
All... nine?

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.340
What is he?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.530
Huh?

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:53.060
Isn't ten the consecutive strike out record for the majors?

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.870
The Hornets failed to score once again in the eleventh inning.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.440
Neither team is letting the other get an edge.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.990
And the highlight of this twelfth inning!

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:13.660
He's consecutively struck out nine batters in the last three innings,

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:19.920
and now he returns to the mound with a chance to break the record for consecutive strike outs.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:27.630
If all goes well, we won't just win, but we'll win with a new record!

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.260
This is amazing!

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.880
Good luck, Shigeno!

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:34.850
Now that we're here, we have to break the record and win!

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:41.780
I'm so glad... I'm a Hornets fan.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.250
Dear—

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.700
Make us proud!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:46.820
Shigeno!

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.220
Shigeno!

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:01.630
We couldn't win for twenty-five years,

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.700
but the fans kept cheering us on.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.300
I want to make them happy.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:11.180
That dream is already well within our reach.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.100
Please, Doctor.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.780
Even if it's just a run, or just a single pitch,

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:19.090
I want to help my team!

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.580
So this...

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.940
This is your answer,

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.590
Shigeno.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.670
Play!

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:46.270
Now, will he tie the record with a tenth strike out?

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:47.840
This first pitch is important.

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:54.410
Strike!

00:06:57.230 --> 00:07:00.850
Damn, I knew it was going to be a fastball.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:04.690
Wow, what a guy.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.150
This can't be right.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.090
I can't believe he has circulatory problems.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:15.530
Do anything you can to hit the ball!

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:21.320
Strike two!

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:55.780
Shigeno! Shigeno! Shigeno!

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:14.140
Out!

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:18.350
Shigeno misses the record by a hair!

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:23.580
Shigeno!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.650
Shigeno!

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:30.920
Goro!

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.320
What's wrong?

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:35.240
Shigeno is down, clutching his arm.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.370
What's going on?

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.450
Honda...

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.150
Time out!

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:41.200
Are you okay?

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:41.200
Shigeno!

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:41.960
Shigeno!

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:46.060
Hey, what's wrong with Shigeno?

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:46.060
Shigeno!

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:47.750
Damn...

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.640
That's it.

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.190
What's wrong, Shigeno?

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:54.600
Are you okay?

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:01.020
Boss, is there anyone ready in the bullpen?

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:05.810
No, but they're starting now.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.460
I see.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.710
Well...

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.320
I'm perfectly fine!

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:21.770
I just sort of tripped, and fell...

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:26.270
But you were holding your arm.

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:27.520
No problem.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:31.450
If I don't do well against the next batter,

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:33.550
please take me out.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.060
It looks like Shigeno is continuing.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.600
He is?!

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.020
Is he all right?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.950
That idiot...

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.640
He's pushing himself again.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.360
What the heck just happened to him?

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:56.780
What are you thinking?

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.440
Are you still going to deceive your coach?

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:01.580
Anyone who saw that pitch would know.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.870
If it's flaring up, get off the mound.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:11.210
No, you've done well with your problems,

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.370
but you've done enough now.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.470
Leave the rest to the other pitchers.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.910
I know, Keene.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.100
I know that.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:26.390
But they're not ready yet,

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:30.480
so I can't just leave the mound because I feel like it.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:33.830
I was the one hiding my condition,

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.590
so I have to take responsibility for my actions.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:40.830
Just one batter's fine.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.650
Please let me buy some time!

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.290
Then don't push yourself anymore.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:57.350
You could even walk him.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:59.490
Just think about buying time.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:10.790
Play!

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.900
Are you kidding me, Keene?

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:20.570
If I give them a walk just to buy time,

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.030
there's no point.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.410
Strike!

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.420
That idiot...

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:37.590
It looks like... he's okay?

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:41.510
He's... doing it again.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:53.430
Goro...

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:14.130
No.

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:15.420
You can't!

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:19.160
You promised that you'd stop if it started hurting!

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.340
Ball!

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:27.100
But he shouldn't even be able to throw with the pain anymore.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:30.680
Strike!

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:35.390
I've come this far.

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:39.980
What the hell am I doing dragging everyone down?!

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:42.280
Foul!

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:46.620
I need to take out this batter, or I'll never live it down!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:50.040
Foul!

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:56.640
You've done enough.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.190
That was plenty of time.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.180
Walk him.

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:06.550
Foul! Foul!

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.620
All right!

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.510
His speed is dropping!

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:12.810
We can finish him!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.230
Shigeno...

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:21.280
What's the point of pushing yourself so far?

00:13:29.110 --> 00:13:31.040
Keep it up, Shigeno!

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.390
Don't lose!

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:46.910
No...

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:50.050
Stop pitching, Shigeno!

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:58.230
For me, as a lover of baseball,

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:05.440
and all my fans around the world who love baseball as much as I do,

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:12.660
I will keep standing on the mound as long as my body can move.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.390
Shields is managing to hold on with these fouls.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.460
And here comes Shigeno's eighth pitch.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.630
Shigeno, show us your guts!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.250
Don't lose!

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.590
Come on, Shigeno.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:25.800
Honda...

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:27.760
Goro...

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.260
Strike out!

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.880
101 here?!

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:25.190
Shigeno, you...

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.480
Amazing!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.220
He's really amazing!

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.280
Yeah.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:39.720
H-Hey...

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.120
Shigeno?

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:59.270
You're an idiot for playing so close to your limit.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:04.520
I'll never understand your way of baseball or your values.

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.780
Hey, what's wrong?

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:11.870
He can't pitch anymore.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:12.700
What?

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:16.600
I see.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.050
Thanks for you work.

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:22.290
Take a nice, long break.

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:25.190
Shigeno.

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:31.260
Leave the rest to us.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.950
We'll win this game no matter what.

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:03.680
That was wonderful pitching, Shigeno.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.440
What's wrong?

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.860
He can still pitch over 100 mph.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:14.870
His arm is hurting.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:19.590
He walked off the mound by himself.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:24.000
He must've been pushing himself.

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:26.840
I hope it doesn't leave any permanent damage.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:28.000
He'll be fine.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:33.880
He hasn't changed at all since he was a kid.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:42.870
He'll come back at full strength.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:44.720
I'm sure of it.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:52.860
Shigeno.

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:57.250
Nice pitching.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:18:01.930
If I could've pitched more, I wouldn't have put so much pressure on you.

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:13.110
Sh-Shigeno!

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.790
Out!

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.670
Nice play, Roy.

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:31.250
What's wrong?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.520
Oh, and?

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:34.550
Is he okay?

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.300
He'll have to be checked at the hospital.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.680
The ambulance is on its way.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:41.920
What happened to Shigeno?

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.000
He's an idiot.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:48.520
Keene, do you know something?

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.610
Circulatory problem?

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.270
That's impossible!

00:18:57.270 --> 00:19:00.340
He was throwing so well!

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:03.700
Keene, why didn't you tell us something that important?

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:13.130
Because, I lost to his spirit...

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:22.920
His spirit to make the Hornets win, no matter what.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:32.690
Shigeno, you haven't changed at all since the first time I met you.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:37.920
Undoubtedly, you're an idiot.

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:44.450
But it'll be pretty fun to start the Hornets' Golden Age

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:45.990
with an idiot like you!

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:49.910
All right!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.750
Nice batting!

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:52.970
We can do this.

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:54.050
We can do this!

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.920
All right, follow Keene!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:59.710
Parker, don't put Shigeno's efforts to waste.

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:11.730
You're gonna show a rookie like me what a real major league play is, right?

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:19.780
In the end, that rookie was the one fueling our spirits all season.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:20.570
What?

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.060
A walk?

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.250
I see.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:29.280
They're going to put him on first and fight with Murdoch, who hasn't hit today.

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.090
Ball! Ball four!

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:38.590
Please, Murdoch.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:46.760
If you're a professional, complain after you've proven yourself to your teammates!{pasted from ep 14}

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:50.020
If you're a man, then pay them back!

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:53.140
You're on the Hornets now, Murdoch!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.330
That's right.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.190
I owe everything to you, Shigeno.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.040
And in the bottom of the twelfth,

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:23.200
the Hornets made the playoffs for the first time in twenty-five years, thanks to Murdoch's home run.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:31.170
Murdoch, you took all the meat and potatoes in the end.

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:37.670
Looks like no champagne fight for me this year.

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:40.540
It's open.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.280
Don't give us that attitude.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.910
Hey, Shigeno.

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:45.570
We came to check up on you.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.450
You're in better shape than I thought.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:49.530
Guys!

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.010
What are you doing here?

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:55.430
And all of you?!

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:59.320
I told them that the hospital wouldn't like it.

00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:00.590
Shut up!

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:05.250
We have to do this to the guy who took part in our victory.

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:11.780
G-Guys...

00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:17.140
For some reason, you left early yesterday.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:19.310
So we decided to come pay you a visit.

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:23.030
I see...

00:22:23.950 --> 00:22:25.290
Thanks.

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:29.530
Wait, we can't have a champagne fight in the hospital!

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:31.350
No, we sure can.

00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:33.290
I brought a plastic sheet.

00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:36.270
Give me a break, you idiots!

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.460
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.460
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:58.180
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:58.180
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.390 --> 00:22:59.850
yume wo

00:22:58.390 --> 00:23:03.020
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:03.020
oikaketeiru

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:05.810
ground no ue ni

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:09.020
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:05.810 --> 00:23:09.020
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:12.990
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:12.990
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:20.410
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:20.410
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:27.710
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:27.710
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:32.460
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:35.480
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:35.480
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:38.090
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:43.140
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:38.090 --> 00:23:39.850
kizukazu ni

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:43.140
suki ni natta

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:45.430
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:50.270
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:45.430 --> 00:23:50.270
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:52.860
zutto mae kara

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:57.950
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:54.740
otagai ni

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:57.950
hikareteita

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:00.160
kono kimochi wa

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:07.160
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:07.160
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:15.280
